  "notes": "The piano-first songwriter-producer of the 2010s radio middle. The compositional order is the documented parameter and it is unusual enough to be worth encoding: he \"started playing piano at age three\" and came to Nashville from a UK pop-artist career, \"and his productions are correspondingly chord-forward — choruses harmonised before they are melodised,\" so `chordToneBias` runs at the top of this batch and the melody sits inside the voicing rather than against it. Harmony is \"I–V–vi–IV, I–IV–V and ii–V turnarounds, plus mixolydian vamps on the acoustic cuts.\" Drums are \"a modern layered kit — programmed clap on the backbeat, 16th shaker, sampled kick under the acoustic kick — with the acoustic cuts dropping to brushes and a two-beat. Half-time bridges and post-chorus drop-outs,\" so the clap layer and the 16th shaker carry the radio setting while the cross-stick flag carries the acoustic one. The palette formula is quoted and is the counter's job: \"real acoustic strings (dobro, banjo, mandolin, fiddle) alive under layered electrics and a piano/synth pad — the 'roots instruments over a pop bed' formula that defined mid-2010s radio.\" Melody is \"mid-tenor, rhythmically busy verses with a wide chorus leap.\" ⚠ The programmed sub is \"reinforcement on the radio cuts\" under a live bass, so no `drums.bass808` block. ⚠ Confidence is medium and the research says why: \"roster, piano-first background and chart record documented; per-session method inferred from the records [LOW-CONF].\" ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the clap offsets, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
